<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rosli Dhobi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1932–1950</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rosli Dhobi was a Sarawak nationalist of the anti-cession movement, which opposed the transfer of Sarawak from the Brooke rajahs to the British crown in 1946. In December 1949, aged 17, he stabbed Governor Duncan Stewart at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sibu">Sibu</a>, and he was hanged in 1950. He is now honoured in Malaysia as a national hero.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rosli-dhobi.jpg" alt="Rosli Dhobi" width="240" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rosli_Dhoby.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
